GPU, storage and machine model all come from one shared `Machine` struct,
populated by JSON-decoding `system_profiler ... -json`. -json was only added
in macOS 10.15, so on every OS version this port targets that call produces
plain text instead of JSON, json.decode() fails, get_misc() returns none,
and all three fields are dropped -- vfetch.v skips any field whose Result is
unsuccessful. system_profiler itself, and the plain-text format each of
these three actions have always used, both predate 10.15 by a long way; only
the -json flag is the problem. Replace each field with an independent,
portable lookup instead of trying to keep the shared JSON call alive:

* machine: hw.model (e.g. "MacBookPro9,2", "PowerMac3,1") via sysctlbyname,
  the same MIB neofetch uses for "Model:" on macOS -- no marketing-name
  lookup table, just the raw identifier.

* storage: os.disk_usage('/'), V's own statvfs(3) wrapper (vlib/os/os_nix.c.v).
  statvfs is a thin libc wrapper around statfs(2) per its own man page, so
  this avoids hand-declaring a `struct statfs`, whose layout differs across
  SDKs depending on _DARWIN_FEATURE_64_BIT_INODE (the same kind of mismatch
  patch-memory-pre-10.9.diff had to work around for vm_statistics64).

* gpu: `system_profiler SPDisplaysDataType -detailLevel mini` in its default
  plain-text form (i.e. the same command with -json simply dropped), parsed
  for the first "Chipset Model:" line -- the same field neofetch's own macOS
  get_gpu() greps for. Kept on its own thread since it's the one field here
  that's still a slow subprocess call; machine and storage are cheap direct
  syscalls so they no longer need one.

--- system/machine.v.original
+++ system/machine.v
@@ -1,14 +1,17 @@
 module system

+#include <sys/types.h>
+#include <sys/sysctl.h>
+
+fn C.sysctlbyname(name &char, oldp voidptr, oldlenp &usize, newp voidptr, newlen u64) int
+
 @[inline]
-fn get_machine(data Machine) Result {
-	if data.hardware.len > 0 {
-		for hardware in data.hardware {
-			if hardware.machine.len > 0 {
-				return success(hardware.machine)
-			}
-		}
-	}
+fn get_machine() Result {
+  mut model := []u8{len: 256}
+  mut len := usize(sizeof(model))
+  if C.sysctlbyname("hw.model".str, &char(model.data), &len, 0, 0) != 0 {
+    return failure
+  }

-	return failure
+  return success(model.bytestr())
 }

